            <ArticleTitle>[Methods of assessing postoperative pain in children].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>60-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study of the evaluation of postoperative pain in 210 children using physiological, reference and observation methods. A comparison with other methods leads to the conclusion that observation is the best choice and that some children do not need analgesics during the postoperative period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
